WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.693
- [Narrator] How would I describe the vibe

00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:05.403
of Cascade on a Sunday night?

00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:10.030
You would see 500, 800,
1,000 people in the facility.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.447
You have this culture
that has been created,

00:00:13.447 --> 00:00:17.177
and it's just growing out of control.

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:18.492
And you don't really experience that

00:00:18.492 --> 00:00:20.575
anywhere else but here.

00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:25.492
(upbeat music leading into choral singing)

00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:28.440
- [Second Narrator]
When desegregation began

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.108
in the late '50s and early '60s,

00:00:30.108 --> 00:00:33.178
some roller rink owners
did not take kindly to it.

00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:35.277
They decided to create themed nights

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:38.125
specifically targeted
towards African-Americans.

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:40.654
If Black roller skaters made
an appearance on other days

00:00:40.654 --> 00:00:43.473
of the week, they found
themselves unwelcome.

00:00:43.473 --> 00:00:45.423
But those nights ended up turning

00:00:45.423 --> 00:00:47.358
into something all of their own.

00:00:47.358 --> 00:00:48.719
- I didn't realize the impact

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:51.411
that a roller skating
rink has on a community.

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:53.574
They would just open up a skating rink,

00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:56.956
and, boy, people came,
and it was always crowded.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.957
So all of those things came together

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.374
to really blow roller skating up.

00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:04.624
Here is what so many people gravitate to.

00:01:04.624 --> 00:01:09.207
And I didn't realize until
I actually built Cascade.

00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:13.398
(upbeat music)

00:01:13.398 --> 00:01:15.344
- I don't know where I would
be without roller skating.

00:01:15.344 --> 00:01:17.552
It saved me.

00:01:17.552 --> 00:01:19.167
So Sunday nights at Cascade

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:21.917
is amazing because of the energy.

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:24.605
We come, you got your crews, you got your

00:01:24.605 --> 00:01:26.913
single skaters, you got your couples,

00:01:26.913 --> 00:01:29.053
and it's time to show out.

00:01:29.053 --> 00:01:30.708
It's the real Atlanta culture.

00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:34.995
And you can kinda see the
style that Atlanta does.

00:01:34.995 --> 00:01:37.174
We call it riding in Atlanta,

00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:39.020
it's just a really cool, like,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.672
you ride the beat and they go fast,

00:01:40.672 --> 00:01:43.951
so we wear the low Carerra
skates with the big speed wheels,

00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:46.101
and you see the guys doing the routines

00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:48.022
and there are a couple of original groups

00:01:48.022 --> 00:01:51.112
that still skate, and that
got the style started.

00:01:51.112 --> 00:01:54.403
The roller skating culture is
like an underground family.

00:01:54.403 --> 00:01:56.018
We have a Facebook, we have a skatebook.

00:01:56.018 --> 00:01:58.794
It's kind of addictive,
it's our drug of choice,

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:00.889
and it's a nonstop party on wheels,

00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:04.639
so that's kind of how
I fell in love with it.

00:02:05.652 --> 00:02:07.181
- Even on a Sunday night, we have people

00:02:07.181 --> 00:02:08.222
that will tell you
they've been skating here

00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:09.813
since they was eight years old.

00:02:09.813 --> 00:02:13.325
It's kinda like the mom, the dad,

00:02:13.325 --> 00:02:16.298
the teenager, the little brother,

00:02:16.298 --> 00:02:18.499
and they all are skating.

00:02:18.499 --> 00:02:21.504
It's just a lifestyle
that when you come here,

00:02:21.504 --> 00:02:24.390
you get the energy of all
different types of people,

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.515
all different types of walk,

00:02:25.515 --> 00:02:28.905
but when they come here, they're skaters.

00:02:28.905 --> 00:02:31.137
So all those things kind of bundle up

00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:33.092
into this building that makes this place,

00:02:33.092 --> 00:02:35.304
to me, what the community would miss

00:02:35.304 --> 00:02:36.762
if this skating rink wasn't here.

00:02:36.762 --> 00:02:39.315
That's why it's been here for
so long, it's still thriving.

00:02:39.315 --> 00:02:40.534
You make it about the community,

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:43.120
everything else just
kind of falls into place.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.453
(upbeat music resolves)

